ew": "Dick Durbin's retirement leaves an open Democratic-held Senate seat in Illinois, a state that leans about six points Democratic at the presidential level. Lieutenant Governor Juliana Stratton faces Republican Don Tracy, with a minor independent also on the ballot. Stratton has raised nearly $6 million and benefits from roughly $9 million in outside support, while Tracy has raised about $2.5 million and is running closely aligned with President Trump in a state where that is a liability.\n\nNo public general-election polling is available, but all ten expert raters place the race in the Safe or Solid Democratic column, and prediction markets uniformly give Stratton a 98% chance of winning. The fundamentals point to a Democratic margin in the mid-teens, consistent with the state's lean and the current national environment.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9877, "margin": 15.07}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9857, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9943, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9883, "margin": 15.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9819, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9928, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9849, "margin": 15.0}]}